  "authority_notes": "Feature-OFF backup composition plus Linear, generic Source, Buzz and Hermes backup-generation contracts. The generic Source binder emits a backup pointer immediately but emits an accepted restore_test only from a separately verified human-acceptance envelope; pending technical restore remains a candidate. Buzz separates Postgres/media/Git/Redis capture, isolated restore, audit, identity recovery and human backup acceptance. Hermes binds Agent Mark/Deployment, runtime/profile, instructions, skills/tools, exact session crosswalk, memory/schedule, backup/restore and acceptance refs while keeping Agent readiness, Task Done and accepted context unevaluated. These public contracts perform no provider/filesystem/runtime/network/clock effect and do not grant source, task, artifact, Agent or completion authority. Actual binding, bytes, service quiescence, restore execution and human acceptance remain separate private gates."
